Spoilers ahoy, then, I guess...

You may want to wait before charging *all* of your wands of death.
Scrolls of charging are invaluable when you're casting spells, because
they refill your energy when you read them while confused.  Take a few
with you to the astrals.

Don't ever take off your ring of free action.  There are lots of things
that can happen that you really don't want to be paralyzed for.  As far
as the ring of protection goes, I'd only try to charge it if it's at +2
or less.  There's a (charges/7) chance of it exploding when you try and
add more charges.

> I want to enchant/fooproof the boots of levitation(I don't want to rely
> on my ring it can explode).
> Is there any adventage to using the fireproofed boots of water walking
> over levitation? Should I even bring them?

No.  There is no water to walk on in the astrals.  

You're right that the levitation boots are less likely to be destroyed
than a ring would be, but the big downside is that it reduces your
speed to Fast from Very Fast when you don't wear speed boots.  That is
why most people go with the ring - the elementals on the plane of air
are very very fast, and you can't engrave elbereth there, and it's just
not a fun place to be in general so it's better to cross it quickly.
There's also the fact that the levitation boots probably aren't going to
be enchanted, but honestly that's not as important as the speed issue.

