They can.  It is a pain in the butt.  The only things you need to worry
about B/C/U on, though, are your bag of holding, blindfold, and unicorn
horn, for the most part.  Rings may also be a concern.

18 holy waters should be more than enough.

> I really think this could be my first acsention, and I want to take it
> slow and think it out. Is my experience level high enough? What about
> my HP? I can revese genocide nurses or wraithes in sokoban again.

Most of that looks fine.  Do you have any potions of full healing
around?  Definitely not a bad idea if you do, especially as a monk.

Two big things are missing there.  One is food.  Famine will make you
hungry, so you need a lot of quick calories in your backpack.  The
quickest calories are C-Rations and K-rations, with C-rations having the
most consumable calories per turn.  I usually take around 20 of them but
I've never been able to figure out why.  15 or so would probably be more
than sufficient.

The second is scrolls of gold detection.  Theoretically you can find the
portals on the astral planes by using the amulet but practically
speaking you want to read a non-cursed scroll of gold detection while
confused and find it immediately.  So make sure you have 4 of those, one
for each plane.

A third thing which isn't quite as crucial is a wand of secret door
detection to find the door at moloch's sanctum.  You can just search the
outer doors for it, but that's a minor pain.

I'm sure I'm forgetting something.  Umm, wands of teleportation.  Don't
engage in hand to hand combat with someone wielding Vorpal Blade if at
all possible, and Mjollnir to a lesser extent.  Don't die, and keep an
eye out for death in all its varied forms.  Good luck!

